  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 2, 'Digital adaptation kits within the SMART guideline continuum'. Five rows: L1 Narrative (narrative guidelines: evidence-based recommendations with implementation and data guidance); L2 Operational (digital adaptation kits: software-neutral documentation of operational and functional requirements such as personas, workflows, metadata, algorithms, minimum data sets and priority metrics); L3 Machine readable (structured software-neutral specifications, code, terminology and interoperability standards); L4 Executable (reference software that executes static algorithms and interoperable components); and L5 Dynamic (precision health models trained and optimised with advanced analytics). Each row passes through a vertical 'Localisation' bar to its country-implementation adaptation: national policies and procedures; localised requirements; localised machine-readable code and standards; localised static digital services within a digital health enterprise; and dynamic applications optimised for local outcomes. A blue arrow beside them runs from 'Paper systems' at the top to 'Smart digital systems' at the bottom. Source: adapted from reference 18.",
